obligation = "Retain the complete capability and qualify its applicable acceptance criteria on the candidate; preserve valid existing implementation and evidence."
do_1 = "Preserve the existing crate platform/hosted/identity (package layerx-platform-identity, binary layerx-identity) in the hosted house style listening on LAYERX_IDENTITY_LISTEN (default 0.0.0.0:9443) with rustls server TLS, a durable fsync-backed store under LAYERX_IDENTITY_STATE_DIR holding principals {sub, allowed_signer_public_keys, account, audiences} and sessions {session_id, principal, token_digest, csrf_digest, csrf_token sealed at rest with the store key, expires_at, revoked_at}, and service tokens from LAYERX_IDENTITY_SERVICE_TOKENS_DIR where each file name is the calling service (gateway, registry, webhooks, dashboard, faucet, testnet, ramp, provisioning, registrar) and the content its token."
do_2 = "Serve POST /v1/principals only for the provisioning or distinct registrar service token; serve POST /v1/sessions and DELETE /v1/sessions/{id} only for provisioning. Mint an opaque session token of the form ses_<id>.<secret> and return the token and csrf_token once. Registrar has principal-creation authority only: it cannot mint, revoke or introspect sessions, bind publication keys or use the registry-only publication-principal resolver. Registry remains distinct from registrar: its existing authenticated publication-principal resolver access grants no principal creation, session management or introspection authority. Preserve every existing service-token refusal, missing or duplicate-token startup refusal, tenant-binding check and negative assertion. Serve POST /v1/sessions/introspect and POST /v1/introspect answering per presented service token exactly the shape that caller parses with Content-Type application/json and no charset - gateway {active, sub, allowed_signer_public_keys}, webhooks and dashboard {active, sub, csrf_token}, faucet and testnet {active, sub}, ramp with audience {active, principal_id, account, audience, expires_at} - inactive for unknown, expired or revoked tokens, constant-time digest comparison, and GET /readyz unauthenticated 200 only when the store is writable, GET /livez."
do_3 = "Write in-crate and platform/hosted/identity/tests coverage for every introspection shape, revocation, expiry, wrong-service-token refusal and store restart; add platform/hosted/identity/Dockerfile from the faucet template and platform/hosted/identity/deployment.yaml (Deployment in layerx-testnet with pod label layerx-plane: trusted-boundary, Service layerx-identity 9443 -> 9443, a state PersistentVolumeClaim, ingress from testnet-control, the faucet, the gateway and the developer namespace, egress DNS only)."
symbols = ["layerx-identity", "session introspection shapes"]
do_4 = "Requirement 1053.3 remains required in full. Identity component qualification proves only its own authenticated service behavior and unauthenticated writable-store readiness contribution; it does not prove global testnet readiness. RELEASE task 103.3.7 owns execution of the complete per-dependency and per-journey readiness contract, and RELEASE task 70.8 includes that complete coverage in its candidate-bound runtime-assembly manifest and evidence validation. Neither requirement 1053.3 nor broader release obligations are discharged by task 103.6.5."

