do_2 = "Implement the public synchronization origin and relay/archive daemon with pinned bootstrap, durable backfill and live synchronization, complete indexed history, peer discovery and exact-byte idempotent forwarding."
do_3 = "Package the daemon with an integrity-pinned installer, systemd/container entry points and operator instructions."
do_4 = "Integrate all seven capabilities in one wave, then run one compile pass and the focused real-process end-to-end gate. Rerun only after a relevant repair, at most twice. Preserve unrelated owner edits and existing gates."
symbols = ["lxp_archive_codec_main", "RelayArchive"]

[req.1062]
title = "Beta Surface Expansion"
story = "As a user or agent choosing LayerX over a general-purpose chain, I want non-fungible assets, k-of-n and time-locked authority, human-readable names, a program-readable price feed, spot swaps, an uncapped token path and self-custody of my own key, so that the things I can do on a general chain I can also do here, while ordering, fees, guarantors and governance stay exactly as the protocol spec locks them."
ac_1 = "THE programs SDK and registry SHALL define an LXT721 non-fungible interface (mint, transfer, approve, set_approval_for_all, owner_of, balance_of, token_uri, total_supply, metadata) next to LXT20, with a reference WASM program, a registry-enforced reference interface and a registry test that mirrors lxt20_reference, and ownership SHALL only change through the program's own storage under its namespace; no protocol change."
ac_2 = "THE authority table SHALL gain two additive kinds: LXP_AUTHORITY_KIND_MULTISIG binding a grant to a k-of-n signer set whose approvals are collected as ordinary signed approvals and resolved by the one common resolver, and LXP_AUTHORITY_KIND_TIMELOCK binding a grant to an earliest-execution sequence or timestamp; existing kinds, encodings, grant ids and resolver results SHALL be byte-identical for existing grants, and a multisig grant below threshold or a timelock before maturity SHALL resolve to a typed refusal, never to success or to an unknown outcome."
ac_3 = "THE programs SDK SHALL ship a naming registry reference program mapping a UTF-8 NFC-normalised name (3-63 chars, [a-z0-9-], no leading or trailing hyphen) to a DID with register, transfer, renew, resolve and reverse-resolve entry points, first-come ownership, an expiry paid in occupancy through fund_program_402, and a registry test; the human explorer lookup SHALL resolve a name through the program read path when present."
ac_4 = "THE programs ABI SHALL allocate guest ABI v3 whose new layerx_v3 namespace holds the single host function oracle_read(market_id, out), leaving the frozen layerx_v2 vector and checksum byte-identical, and oracle_read SHALL return the latest committed perps oracle observation (price, timestamp, sequence, source set digest) for a market from the oracle store the batch header already commits under oracle_root, refusing with a typed result when the market is unknown or halted; validate.rs, ABI_MANIFEST, the C host binding, the Rust SDK wrapper and programs-abi-drift SHALL all agree, and a native test SHALL prove a program reads the same observation the perps engine used."
ac_5 = "THE programs SDK SHALL ship a constant-product swap reference program over two LXT20 tokens or one LXT20 token and one 402LXP asset with add_liquidity, remove_liquidity, swap_exact_in, quote and reserves entry points, LP shares as an LXT20 program token, all value moved only through transfer_program_402 and program_call to the LXT20 programs, a slippage bound the caller supplies and a conservation test in programs/tests/conservation; the program holds no authority beyond its own derived account."
ac_6 = "THE asset registry SHALL hold at least 1024 assets: LX_ASSET_REGISTRY_CAPACITY rises to 1024 with the state encoding, reserve attestation, genesis builder and every static array sized from it updated so that existing fixtures with fewer than 64 assets decode byte-identically and test-asset-registry, test-asset-reserve and the genesis builder pass; the gateway lx_listAssets SHALL paginate."
ac_7 = "THE human service SHALL make self-custody the default posture: onboarding SHALL offer key export as the first path and custodial holding as an explicit opt-in; export SHALL be a step-up ceremony in the secret-reveal class bound to one operation digest that returns the DID primary key exactly once, records a durable audit event, and marks the identity self-custodied so the KMS refuses to sign for it afterwards; the existing no-key-export suite SHALL be rewritten to assert that export happens only through this ceremony and never through any other route, and spec/layerx-platform/spec.kvx [contract_context.103.decision] custody and v1_scope SHALL be updated to state the new default."
contract_profile = "retained-with-explicit-resolutions"
reference_namespace = "feature.103"

