[req.1063]
title = "Paxeer X Fork Surface"
story = "As a wallet, trader, token creator, bridge user or agent on Paxeer X, I want the exchange, bridge, launchpad and account history to be native to the chain on the Paxeer side and served by the LayerX kernel and services on the LayerX side, so that one account, one seed and one data source cover both halves of the network without Solidity middlemen or trusted upgrade keys."
ac_1 = "THE Paxeer node SHALL expose a layerxexchange precompile at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001015 backed by a layerxexchange module: depositMargin, withdrawMargin, placeOrder, cancelOrder and requestSettlement SHALL move funds only through the layerxcustody module account and SHALL emit typed ABI events plus Cosmos typed events that the LayerX intent router consumes; getMarket, getOrder, getPosition and getMargin SHALL read finalized LayerX state through the anchor's finalizedStateRoot with a state proof and never over the network; no matching logic SHALL exist on Paxeer."
ac_2 = "THE Paxeer node SHALL expose a layerxbridge precompile at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001016 backed by a layerxbridge module holding a per-chain registry (chain id, vault address, finality depth, enabled flag), a bonded attestor set with threshold, per-asset caps and a global pause; an inbound transfer SHALL mint a tokenfactory denom under the module admin only when threshold attestor signatures over (chain, vault, tx hash, log index, recipient, asset, amount) verify and the nullifier is unused; an outbound transfer SHALL burn the denom and emit BridgeOut for the relayer; every cap SHALL default to zero and the registry SHALL be empty at genesis so the bridge ships dormant; registry, attestor and cap changes SHALL be x/gov messages."
ac_3 = "THE Paxeer node SHALL expose a launchpad precompile at 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001017 backed by a launchpad module implementing the KindleLaunch core natively: createMarket mints a fixed-supply tokenfactory denom with an ERC20 pointer and opens a virtual-reserve constant-product curve; buy and sell apply ReserveLib and FeeLib semantics (base fee plus age decay plus volatility over an 8-slot snapshot ring, clamped) with the virtual floor; fees split protocolFeeBps to the treasury module account and the rest to the market's fee-rights holder under one of claim, burn, airdrop or lp-rewards; quoteBuy, quoteSell, getReserves, getPrice, getPriceSnapshots, getMarket, getMarkets and getMarketsByCreator SHALL be views; config lives in module params changed only by x/gov; opticals, router, quoter and the fee NFT remain EVM contracts and are out of scope for v6.6."
ac_4 = "THE v6.6 upgrade SHALL add the layerxexchange, layerxbridge and launchpad store keys in the existing v6.6 StoreUpgrades block of node/app.go, register the three keepers in node/precompiles.go, list the three precompiles in precompiles/setup.go through generated setup.go files, and a node upgrade test SHALL prove a chain at v6.4.0 state loads under v6.6 with the three stores added and all three precompiles callable."
ac_5 = "THE LayerX perps kernel module SHALL make matched fills the only source of positions: execute_order_place SHALL open, increase or reduce the taker's and makers' positions at the fill price, POSITION_OPEN SHALL no longer accept a caller-supplied entry_notional, and every fill price SHALL be within the market's oracle deviation limit of the latest committed oracle observation or the order SHALL be refused with a typed result; existing receipts and event codes 0x0601 to 0x060b SHALL keep their encoding."
ac_6 = "THE LayerX kernel SHALL gain a spot module (module id 7, LXP_MODULE_SPOT) reusing the perps price-time book for two-asset limit and market orders with immediate settlement of both legs through the asset module, ordinals 0x00070001 to 0x00070005 (MARKET_CREATE, ORDER_PLACE, ORDER_CANCEL, MARKET_HALT, MARKET_RESUME), a receipt transfer set per fill, and a conservation test; capacity limits SHALL be compile-time constants."
ac_7 = "THE intent router in layerx-intents SHALL map the layerxexchange, layerxbridge and launchpad precompile events to signed LayerX activities and back, and the TypeScript and Python agent SDKs SHALL ship typed helpers for every write in ac_1 to ac_3 and for perps and spot activities, so that a human through the EVM ABI and an agent through the SDK reach the same state transition."
ac_8 = "THE interop workspace SHALL ship a layerx-bridge-relayer service that watches a registered external chain through the layerx-migrate RPC quorum verifiers, signs attestations through layerx-mirror-signer so chain keys never enter the relayer, submits them to the 0x1016 precompile, and executes BridgeOut releases against the Ethereum vault; and interop/contracts/ethereum-bridge SHALL hold a PaxeerXVault contract with deposit, release under threshold attestor signatures, per-asset caps, pause and a nullifier set, with forge tests."
ac_9 = "THE platform SHALL ship a layerx-indexer service that ingests LayerX through the relay_archive sync protocol and Paxeer through EVM blocks, logs and CometBFT tx_search, decodes every LayerX receipt field set and every precompile and typed module event into a durable SQLite store of per-account, per-asset rows (height or sequence, counterparty, asset, amount, kind, decoded payload), and the gateway SHALL expose lx_getHistory, px_getHistory and px_getUnifiedHistory with cursors and asset metadata, with typed SDK bindings, as the single wallet data source."
ac_10 = "THE fork SHALL be rehearsed before it is run: a script SHALL export mainnet state from a synced full node, start a disposable single-validator chain from it on the current binary, schedule the v6.6 upgrade at a height, swap to the v6.6 binary at the halt and prove the chain resumes with the three new stores and every precompile answering; the runbook SHALL name the halt height, the UTC time, the binary sha256 and the per-validator steps."
ac_11 = "THE indexer SHALL backfill Paxeer history before the fork from the paxscan Blockscout Postgres (blocks, transactions, logs, token_transfers, internal_transactions, tokens) read-only through a connection URL from the environment, normalize every row into the same per-account, per-asset history rows the live EVM ingester writes, fill every height missing from paxscan from a node's EVM JSON-RPC, verify each backfilled block's hash against the node, stop at a fixed finalized cutover height and hand the live ingester a cursor at that height so no row is duplicated or skipped; the ingester SHALL treat a node whose CometBFT tx index is off as EVM-only without failing."
ac_12 = "THE gateway and the human web app SHALL bring each fork surface online only when the chain answers for it: the gateway SHALL probe eth_getCode at the exchange, bridge and launchpad precompile addresses, expose the result as a capabilities method, refuse the write methods of an absent surface with a typed error, and the web app SHALL render history and read-only pages before the fork and switch the launchpad, exchange and bridge write paths on from the capabilities answer without a redeploy."
ac_13 = "THE fork SHALL be driven on chain by governance: a software-upgrade proposal named v6.6 at the halt height whose voting period ends before the halt, a script that submits it, votes from every validator and confirms the scheduled plan, and a consensus-parameter proposal that lowers timeout commit (bypass on) and timeout vote to the values the latency benchmark proves, both with deposits, tallies and abort conditions written into the runbook."
contract_profile = "retained-with-explicit-resolutions"
reference_namespace = "feature.103"

