do_1 = "Switch the Redis certificate and the gateway's outbound root in one deploy window, because the gateway takes one outbound DER root and cannot verify Redis between two deploys: when the served chain of the Redis app of human/wallet/deploy/redis.toml does not end at the internal CA root, issue its certificate through the gateway-redis row of tools/bringup/ca.sh with the Redis app's .internal name by the several-machine path of ca_issue, because the Redis image reads its key from a [[files]] secret, and stage REDIS_TLS_CERT, REDIS_TLS_KEY and REDIS_TLS_CA with flyctl secrets import --stage; then import ENDPOINT_OUTBOUND_CA as the internal CA root on the endpoint app, deploy the Redis app on its new certificate and at once deploy the endpoint app of do_2, so the gateway's one outbound root serves both Redis and the kernel backends."
do_2 = "Make human/wallet/deploy/endpoint.toml run the gateway in kernel mode on its plain listener: core_agent_boundary and independent_receipt_authority at the kernel app's .internal name over mTLS with the client identity issued through the gateway-client row of tools/bringup/ca.sh and imported as Fly secrets, ENDPOINT_OUTBOUND_CA the internal CA root, LAYERX_GATEWAY_PAXEER_RPC_URLS naming at least two serving RPC names that the rpc-nodes subcommand shows at the head, the existing Redis app, and at least two machines in two regions, with LAYERX_GATEWAY_PROGRAM_REGISTRY_URL the registry app's .internal name on port 9420 and LAYERX_GATEWAY_PROGRAM_REGISTRY_TOKEN_FILE the [[files]] token task 2.6 imports, because the gateway's kernel mode requires the registry whenever the component URL is set, so the router's kernel-mode deploy follows the registry app of task 2.6 in the deploy order; add every new [env] name to human/wallet/deploy/env with one line each and deploy it."
do_3 = "Register the router URL on the edge with tools/bringup/edge.sh add api-mainnet-beta.paxeer.network <app>; the app's fly.dev name is the edge's upstream only and is written nowhere else."
do_4 = "Add the router subcommand: through the router URL eth_chainId 0x7d, px_getNetwork kernel.available true, lx_getAccount answering a read for a bound account and /readyz with every configured backend up, and the Redis round trip reported from a machine in each region; then the wallet gateway's /readyz reporting its rpc pool up with the router URL first in its RPC_URLS."
do_5 = "Only after the router checks of do_4 pass: set HYPERPAXEER_RPC_URL to https://api-mainnet-beta.paxeer.network and RPC_URLS to the router URL followed by the serving RPC names on the wallet gateway app of human/wallet/deploy/gateway.toml with flyctl secrets import on standard input from the operator host, which restarts its machines, and update both lines of human/wallet/deploy/env to say so."
