do_1 = "For separately authorized deployment, build both images from the repository root using capability.109.1.1 and capability.109.1.2 build_command, tag the runner image registry.fly.io/paxeer-ci-runners:<source-commit>, authenticate to the registry and push it. Inventory current CI before deciding deployment; create an app-scoped runner deploy token, configure GITHUB_TOKEN, FLY_API_TOKEN and RUNNER_IMAGE as controller secrets, and deploy from the repository root with tools/flyci/controller/fly.toml. Controller credentials remain confined. Confirm one started controller and a completed poll; changing CI_LINUX_RUNNER to fly-linux is a separate authorized deployment step."
do_2 = "Run the current check_ci contract only under authorized integrated qualification: check one started controller and the existing CI_LINUX_RUNNER label; dispatch runner-canary.yml on the default branch using the REST dispatch response workflow_run_id; require the exact run, branch, workflow path and current candidate head_sha; read that run's paginated REST jobs and require completed success with a positive runner_id and runner_name starting with fly-. Preserve the 1500-second wait and cancellation of unfinished runs. Confirm through the Machines API that the actual assigned job machine is removed, following req.210; provisioning-trigger metadata alone is insufficient."
do_3 = "Retain command, source revision, exit code and log location in private qualification evidence referenced by the consolidated spec. Historical deployment evidence remains historical; this source recipe check neither deploys nor changes CI_LINUX_RUNNER, and does not certify a canary execution."
symbols = ["CI_LINUX_RUNNER", "paxeer-ci-controller", "paxeer-ci-runners"]

