do_1 = "the web reader's call reaches the kernel and produces no receipt the core can wait on because the batch planner refuses the schedule item the same batch just minted - with the scheduling identity of task 2.43 in place, lxp_kernel_batch_schedule_item in src/protocol/lxp_kernel.c mints that item with its admission, decode, validate, schedule decode, payer lookup and item preparation all answering LXP_OK, and layerx_programs_schedule_plan answers LXP_ERR_NON_CANONICAL for that one item, because prepare_schedule_item in programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/ffi_call.rs reads the call's grants through CapabilitySet::admitted_schedule_accesses, whose ABI match in programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/abi/capability.rs admits the version 1 and version 2 canonical grant encodings alone and refuses every other version, while the reference web reader declares guest ABI 4 in programs/sdk/rust/examples/web-reader/LayerX.toml and WEB_READER_GUEST_ABI of platform/hosted/gateway/tests/local/events.rs, and the execution that follows the plan decodes the very same grants of the very same call through the ABI-two encoding for ABI 2, 3 and 4 in layerx_programs_call_begin; the batch therefore settles the call as a terminal rejection carrying result code -3, which the core cannot surface because verify_program_outcome of agent/crates/layerx-proof/src/receipt.rs requires a program outcome on a refusal receipt, so POST /v1/programs/call answers 503 receipt_unavailable. The deadline is not the defect - the kernel published that rejection inside a quarter of a second of the submission, and the status assertion of events.rs:475 and LAYERX_CORE_RECEIPT_DEADLINE_MS both stay exactly as they are written."
do_2 = "Add the binding to programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/abi_policy.rs, the module that already holds the frozen ABI transition policy: a CapabilityEncoding naming the ABI-one and ABI-two canonical grant encodings, a capability_encoding answering the encoding an admitted ABI version carries - version 1 the first and versions 2, 3 and 4 the second - refusing any other version with that module's own AbiVersionRefusal::Unsupported, and an abi_version answering the version a validated AbiRevision records; admit no version admit_abi_version refuses and refuse none it admits."
do_3 = "Read that one binding at both projections of the same call - CapabilitySet::admitted_schedule_accesses in programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/abi/capability.rs, which the CALL scheduling projection reaches through prepare_schedule_item, and the grant decode of layerx_programs_call_begin in programs/crates/layerx-programs-runtime/src/ffi_call.rs, which executes the call the plan placed - keeping both refusals exactly as strict as they are, an unadmitted ABI version staying AbiError::InvalidEncoding at the projection and LXP_ERR_NON_CANONICAL at the execution; change no decoder, no capability tag, nothing in the kernel and nothing in the proof crate."
do_4 = "Pin the binding in abi_policy's own unit tests, which the programs workspace test runs: admit_abi_version and capability_encoding accept exactly the same versions across the whole one-byte range, so no ABI can be admitted without a capability encoding; versions 1, 2, 3 and 4 select the v1, v2, v2 and v2 encodings and version 5 is refused as unsupported; and every AbiRevision's recorded version selects the encoding that revision itself carries. The real path stays the task's own gate, whose program call is a guest ABI 4 call into the reference web reader."
do_5 = "Run the verify_cmd once; at the revision where it exits 0 record tasks 2.42, 2.40, 2.37, 2.35 and 2.28 done with that revision, command, exit code and log path and close observations 2.21.2, 2.28.1, 2.35.2, 2.37.2, 2.40.1 and 2.42.1 naming it, as task 2.42's do_5, task 2.40's do_4, task 2.37's do_5 and task 2.35's do_4 require; if it does not pass, leave those five tasks as they are and record the exact failing step as one observation."
