do_6 = "Authorize verified client leaves by an exact URI SAN role: urn:layerx:webhooks:role:producer plus the source bearer permits only event publication; urn:layerx:webhooks:role:operator plus the distinct operator bearer permits only dispatch. Require clientAuth and exactly one recognized role marker. Reject missing, duplicate, contradictory, unknown, malformed or incompatible role markers; never infer a role from CN, headers, bearer alone or generic internal-CA membership. Use structural X.509 parsing and preserve all canonical event and persistence checks."
do_7 = "Extend the existing internal-CA issuer with fixed webhook-operator-client local issuance: issue-local webhook-operator-client --output-dir <absolute-private-directory> and local-services discovery. Keep local identities outside the Fly services roster. Permit no caller-selected identity, role, EKU, SAN or CA override. Refuse existing destinations, symlink components, insecure parent ownership/modes and overlap with CA storage before generation. Publish a complete verified bundle atomically without overwrite from protected staging, with directory mode0700 and files0600; no Fly staging or operator private-key service mounts. Exercise real issuance and refusal paths in the focused harness without printing private material."
do_8 = "Add the producer role SAN only to the existing human-event-client, gateway-client and registry-event-client issuance policies, retaining their identities, trust and bearer interfaces. Keep operator credentials separate. Reconcile retained Kubernetes producer issuance with the same role contract. Prove fail-closed coordinated certificate/token rotation and durable restart; roleless previous leaves must not gain a compatibility bypass."
