do_1 = "Reconcile the retained capability against the current candidate and explicit resolution sections. Reuse conforming implementation; complete only unmet criteria. Resolve historical paths against the current source without narrowing the capability or repeating operational transitions already completed."
do_2 = "Add the crate platform/hosted/core (package layerx-platform-core, binary layerx-core-boundary) in the hosted house style - std TcpListener, rustls server TLS from DER cert and PKCS#8 DER key, hand-framed HTTP/1.1, no tokio - opening two listeners: LAYERX_CORE_LISTEN (default 0.0.0.0:9443) and LAYERX_CORE_ADMIN_LISTEN (default 0.0.0.0:9444), each with its own certificate, the core listener accepting an optional client certificate chaining to LAYERX_CORE_CLIENT_CA_DER."
do_3 = "Back the core listener with layerx-client over the LNI socket named by LAYERX_CORE_LNI_SOCKET and with the daemon's loopback program listener named by LAYERX_CORE_NODE_URL and LAYERX_CORE_NODE_BEARER_TOKEN_FILE: serve GET /readyz (unauthenticated, 200 with {ready, network_id, wire_version, synchronous_receipts, state_snapshot} only when the handshake, the replica and the durable log are live), GET /livez, GET /v1/sequencer, POST /v1/activities (application/octet-stream canonical bytes or {activity: hex}, submit over the LNI once per idempotency key, answer {state, activity_id, batch_id, global_sequence, result_code, state_root, receipt} from the returned receipt, 202 on unknown outcome), GET /v1/receipts/{activity_id}, GET /v1/state, GET /v1/accounts, POST /v1/programs/call, POST /v1/programs/simulate, GET /v1/programs/activities/{id}, GET /v1/programs/receipts/by-idempotency/{key}, GET /v1/programs/registry and /v1/programs/registry/{id}[/interface], and relay the five daemon account-state GET routes unchanged; when the LNI advertises no capability for a route answer 503 {error: {code: capability_unavailable}} and never execute a transition in-process."
do_4 = "Back the admin listener with LAYERX_CORE_ADMIN_TOKEN_FILE, LAYERX_CORE_TREASURY_KEY_FILE and the supervisor socket LAYERX_CORE_SUPERVISOR_SOCKET: POST /admin/v1/testnet/fund validates {funding_id, did, public_key, amount}, resolves the account, builds and signs a SEND from the treasury with layerx-intents and layerx-crypto, submits it over the LNI, answers 200 {funding_id, state: funded, transaction_id} from the receipt and 4xx with a typed code for admin refusals caused by the request; durable-storage faults (journal write or lock failure) answer 503 with no state change; POST /admin/v1/testnet/reset with body {} sends reset to the supervisor and answers 200 {state: reset, reset_id}; both require Idempotency-Key and return the first outcome for a repeated key from a durable idempotency journal under LAYERX_CORE_STATE_DIR."
do_5 = "Write tests under platform/hosted/core/tests that start a real layerxd and replica from build/bin through platform/hosted/node/bootstrap.sh, drive every route over TLS with the beta CA shape, prove funding produces a receipt-verified balance, prove the repeated Idempotency-Key does not move value twice, prove /readyz is 503 while the daemon is down, and add platform/hosted/core/Dockerfile from the faucet template."
