do_1 = "Reconcile the retained capability against the current candidate and explicit resolution sections. Reuse conforming implementation; complete only unmet criteria. Resolve historical paths against the current source without narrowing the capability or repeating operational transitions already completed."
do_2 = "Add the crate platform/hosted/authority (package layerx-platform-authority, binary layerx-receipt-authority) in the hosted house style listening on LAYERX_AUTHORITY_LISTEN (default 0.0.0.0:9445) with rustls server TLS accepting an optional client certificate, authenticating the gateway, registry and webhooks bearer tokens from LAYERX_AUTHORITY_TOKEN_FILES, and dialing only the replica at LAYERX_AUTHORITY_REPLICA_URL (loopback) with LAYERX_AUTHORITY_REPLICA_BEARER_TOKEN_FILE and LAYERX_AUTHORITY_REPLICA_ID, plus the receipt source at LAYERX_AUTHORITY_RECEIPT_URL for receipt bytes by activity id."
do_3 = "Serve GET /v1/authorized-batches/by-activity/{activity_id} and GET /internal/v1/activities/{activity_id}/authority: fetch the canonical receipt for the activity, compute its digest, fetch the replica's batch evidence, verify the header signature and the Merkle inclusion with layerx-proof, re-derive batch_id with layerx_wire::hash::execution_batch_id and require it to equal the receipt's, and answer the eight fields {activity_id, batch_id, asset, previous_state_root, resulting_state_root, sequencer_public_key, network_id, wire_version}, plus batch_evidence only when the batch carries an occupancy-maintenance receipt, containing the maintained batch identity and proof the consumer verifies with Content-Type application/json and no charset; relay GET /v1/batches/{batch_id}/receipt-authority?receipt_digest= to the replica unchanged; serve GET /readyz with {ready, network_id, wire_version} and 200 for an unauthenticated probe only when the replica answers; 404 for an unknown activity, 503 with a typed code when the replica or receipt source is unavailable."
