do_1 = "Reconcile the retained capability against the current candidate and explicit resolution sections. Reuse conforming implementation; complete only unmet criteria. Resolve historical paths against the current source without narrowing the capability or repeating operational transitions already completed."
do_2 = "Add the crate platform/hosted/agent-boundary (package layerx-platform-agent-boundary, binary layerx-agent-boundary) in the hosted house style listening on LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_LISTEN (default 0.0.0.0:9446) with rustls server TLS that accepts an optional client certificate chaining to LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_CLIENT_CA_DER, two distinct bearer tokens from LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_GATEWAY_TOKEN_FILE and LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_REGISTRY_TOKEN_FILE with per-token route entitlement, an LNI client over LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_LNI_SOCKET and the daemon program listener at LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_NODE_URL."
do_3 = "Serve the component contract exactly as the gateway parses it: GET /readyz (bearer or unauthenticated, {ready, network_id, wire_version, synchronous_receipts, state_snapshot}), POST /v1/activities and POST /v1/programs/call taking application/octet-stream canonical bytes with Idempotency-Key, submitting over the LNI exactly once per key from a durable journal under LAYERX_AGENT_BOUNDARY_STATE_DIR, answering 200 {result: {state, activity_id, receipt, terminal_payload, call_graph}} from the receipt, 202 when the outcome is unknown, 4xx carrying the typed refusal; POST /v1/programs/simulate answering {result: {execution, simulation_evidence}} when the LNI provides simulation and a typed 503 capability_unavailable otherwise; GET /v1/programs/activities/{id} with program_id; GET /v1/receipts/{id} as {result: {activity_id, receipt}} and 404 when unknown; GET /internal/v1/receipts/{id} for the developer plane; and the five account-state GET routes relayed to the daemon for the registry token."
