do_2 = "Declare the proposal in api/layerxgov/proposal.proto after api/layerxbridge/proposal.proto: a LayerXProposal message carrying a title, a description and a repeated google.protobuf.Any of the messages it executes, and generate modules/layerxgov/types/proposal.pb.go."
do_3 = "Write modules/layerxgov/types/keys.go with the module name and the router key, and modules/layerxgov/types/proposal.go implementing govtypes.Content and cdctypes.UnpackInterfacesMessage on the generated type: the proposal type constant, its registration with the governance proposal type registry, the amino registration of the content and of every message it may carry, a constructor that packs messages under their type URLs, GetMessages, UnpackInterfaces and String."
do_4 = "In the same file write the accepted-message table: one function that returns the authority of a message the proposal may carry and refuses every other message, covering the authority messages of the custody, anchor, exchange, bridge, launchpad and web-search modules, and a ValidateBasic that refuses an empty title, an empty description, a proposal with no message, a message that fails its own ValidateBasic and a message whose authority is not the governance module account that executes it."
do_5 = "Write modules/layerxgov/handler.go: NewProposalHandler takes the application's message service router, and for each carried message in submission order it looks the handler up by the message's type URL and calls it, returning the first error unchanged so the governance keeper's cached context discards the whole proposal, and refusing a content type that is not the proposal."
do_6 = "Write modules/layerxgov/client/cli/tx.go in the shape of the bridge module's: the layerx-proposal subcommand of paxd tx gov submit-proposal that reads one proposal file, the REST handler beside it, and the client proposal handler that mounts both; register that handler in the application's governance proposal handler list and add the route in node/app.go beside the bridge module's route."
do_7 = "Write modules/layerxgov/types/proposal_test.go over the real message types: a proposal carrying one authority message of each of the six modules validates and returns its messages in order; a message with another authority, a message no module owns, an empty message list and a proposal without a title are each refused; and the content survives a marshal and unmarshal through an interface registry. Write node/gov_layerx_test.go on the real application: the route resolves the proposal's router key, the handler executes a proposal that carries two messages of two different modules and leaves both effects in state, a proposal whose second message fails leaves neither effect, and the submit subcommand is on the built command tree."
