[task.111.5.4]
title = "Migrate the production wallets with the ceremony tool"
status = "pending"
mode = "BUILD"
wave = 4
requires = ["0.2", "111.5.2", "13.1", "13.3"]
reqs = ["1207.1", "1207.2", "1207.4", "1207.5", "1209.2", "1209.5"]
do_1 = "Reconcile the retained capability against the current candidate and explicit resolution sections. Reuse conforming implementation; complete only unmet criteria. Resolve historical paths against the current source without narrowing the capability or repeating operational transitions already completed."
do_2 = "Add a move subcommand to human/wallet/ceremony/cmd/ceremony/main.go, in a new internal/move package, over the source-mode copy of task 5.2 (CopySource, checkReadOnlyRole, TableCounts and PrepareSchema): it reads the production wallet database through the read-only role named by the source connection variable of 5.2 in one REPEATABLE READ READ ONLY transaction and streams every table with COPY TO STDOUT into COPY FROM STDIN on the gateway's platform database named by CEREMONY_DATABASE_URL, which must hold no gateway table before the move starts; it never writes to the source, never creates a file, and leaves the production database and the old service running; before the remaining gateway migrations run it records, for every table, the row count and the SHA-256 digest of the COPY stream ordered by primary key on the source and of the same columns re-read in the same order from the target, refuses to finish when a count or a digest differs, and prints counts and digests only."
do_3 = "Give move a --delta mode for rows written on the old service between the copy's snapshot and the proxy switch: after task 5.3's apply script points the endpoint at the new gateway, it reads the production counts again read-only and copies, in a new single snapshot, only rows whose primary key is absent from the target, refusing and reporting a row whose primary key exists on both sides with different content or whose address or owner and kind collide with a row the new gateway created; the deliver and backfill steps then run again for the rows it moved."
do_4 = "Run the live steps from the operator machine in this order, each only after the check before it passed: move; plan against CEREMONY_DATABASE_URL, whose wallets, eligible and funded counts must equal the rehearsal's; archive, whose row count and file digest must agree with plan; deliver against the deployed attestors inside the ceremony window with the old master key from CEREMONY_MASTER_KEY, which writes migrated_at and attestor_key_id through MarkMigrated only into the gateway's platform database and never into production, and marks a wallet only after the operator verification signature of task 4.13 recovers its address; then deliver --report-only-counts, which must report every eligible wallet migrated. The funded wallets archive into the verified archive and stay marked archived in the gateway's database."
do_5 = "Add a backfill command entry to human/wallet/gateway, since backfillAccounts has none today: src/jobs/backfillAccounts.ts builds the provisioning dependencies with provisionDepsFromEnv, refuses to start without the attestor configuration, calls backfillAccounts in bounded batches from its resumable cursor until done, and prints one totals line per BackfillOutcome (bound, awaiting_owner, awaiting_agent_signature, refused, skipped, failed) with no address, identifier or token; package.json gains a backfill:accounts script over the built entry taking --batch-size and --max-batches. Run once after deliver, it generates each moved wallet's Ed25519 identity and, with no user token present, leaves standard wallets awaiting their owner and agent wallets awaiting their agent's signature; it never signs for an absent user."
do_6 = "Complete each moved wallet's binding at its user's next sign-in: requestAccounts in human/wallet/sdk/src/provider.ts provisions only when /v1/wallet/me answers no_wallet today, so it also posts /v1/wallet/provision with the user's token when /v1/wallet/me returns a wallet whose binding_state is unbound or pending; provisionAccount then resumes from the backfilled identity, sends the sponsor top-up of task 3.1 for the exact binding gas within the cap, has the binding signed through the attestors and broadcasts bindLayerX; a refused binding surfaces as a typed error and a bound wallet makes no provision call."
do_7 = "Add tests: internal/move/move_test.go against a real source database with a read-only role and an empty target, proving counts and digests on both sides, the refusal of a non-empty target, an unchanged source, no file created, and --delta moving only absent rows and refusing a colliding row; human/wallet/gateway/test/backfill-command.test.ts running the entry against the provisioning test's real attestor daemon and in-test chain, asserting the totals line and that no top-up or binding is sent; and provider tests for the provision call on unbound and pending, none on bound, and the typed refusal."
do_8 = "After the backfill, apply task 5.3's proxy on the current host, run move --delta and, when it moved rows, deliver and the backfill entry again; shut the old service down with task 5.3's retire script only after scripts/wallet/check-live.sh cutover passes and the gateway serves the moved wallets; keep the old master key sealed and never destroy it; no step of this task writes to the production database. Steps 4, 5, 8 and 9 of human/wallet/docs/cutover.md name the move, the counts flag and the backfill entry in place of the notes on observations 4.5.4 and 4.5.6."
do_9 = "Append one gate record per step to spec/paxeer-x-wallet/qualification.kvx: the per-table row counts and stream digests on both sides of the move and of any delta, the plan counts beside the rehearsal's, the archive's row count and digest, the deliver report and its --report-only-counts line, the backfill totals with the number awaiting their owner and awaiting an agent signature, the transaction hash of a verified signature from one migrated wallet of each class, the cutover check and the retire run; never an address, a key or a host."
do_10 = "Provide this task selector in tools/paxeer-x/gates and execute the full scoped acceptance contract using real production paths. Preserve the retained verification command coverage; move aggregate matrices to release scope and refuse an unknown or unimplemented selector."
touches = ["human/wallet/ceremony/cmd/ceremony/main.go", "human/wallet/ceremony/cmd/ceremony/main_test.go", "human/wallet/ceremony/internal/move/move.go", "human/wallet/ceremony/internal/move/move_test.go", "human/wallet/ceremony/internal/testsupport/postgres.go", "human/wallet/gateway/src/jobs/backfillAccounts.ts", "human/wallet/gateway/package.json", "human/wallet/gateway/test/backfill-command.test.ts", "human/wallet/sdk/src/provider.ts", "human/wallet/sdk/test/provider.test.ts", "human/wallet/docs/cutover.md", "spec/paxeer-x/qualification.kvx", "tools/paxeer-x/gates/111.5.4.sh"]
