[req.213]
title = "Produce reusable source-bound registry build and isolation artifacts"
ac_1 = "A reusable producer constructs the real registry builder rootfs and runtime base image from identified clean committed source using the existing canonical recipes, then binds source revision/tree, immutable image IDs, canonical environment-tree digest and actual registry, cgroup-supervisor and isolation-executable digests in a protected versioned manifest. Missing, dirty, mismatched or unproven inputs are refused; credential values are never collected or hashed."
ac_2 = "The lifecycle interface allocates only caller-owned disposable resources: bounded ext4 loop-backed build slots with existing per-slot byte and inode ceilings, distinct filesystem identity, nosuid/nodev/noatime options and UID/GID4030 mode0700; and an owned cgroup-v2 container boundary with cpu, memory, pids and io controllers. Existing production startup root-to4030 irreversible privilege-drop, attach-before-exec, no-new-privileges and kill-tree contracts remain unchanged."
ac_3 = "The focused contract executes the actual built cgroup supervisor and isolation executable with real owned processes. It proves cgroup attachment before workload execution, configured memory/PID/CPU/wall and filesystem byte/inode ceilings, bounded termination and complete descendant cleanup; wrong source, wrong digest, missing artifact, unusable quota/cgroup boundary and interrupted lifecycle are refused with no credited ready fixture."
ac_4 = "Prepare, inspect, resume and cleanup use versioned private lifecycle records containing actual owned container/cgroup/mount/loop identities and outcomes. Restart reconciles retained owned state without claiming an unobserved resource; cleanup drains only owned processes, unmounts only the recorded private slots and verifies loop/cgroup release. Partial cleanup remains explicit and blocks reuse; no host-root remount, global service installation or broad cleanup is permitted."
ac_5 = "The producer manifest and verified lifecycle are reusable inputs for real served registry and router qualification. They do not assert healthy registry, authenticated routes, event delivery, durable verification semantics or complete hosted readiness; tasks15.3,16.2 and17.1 retain every original acceptance criterion and gate, including their actual service dependencies."

