[req.215]
title = "Canonical independently authenticated oracle transport with legacy replay isolation"
ac_1 = "Keep lx_oracle_observation_encode/sign and the canonical 72-byte observation body, v1 signature domain, legacy Perps ABI1 decoder/validation, oracle state serialization and all legacy public encoders byte-compatible."
ac_2 = "Introduce exactly137-byte transport version1: byte0=1, bytes1..72=unchanged canonical observation body, bytes73..136=64-byte oracle-observation signature; no padding, trailing bytes, unknown versions or ambiguous lengths."
ac_3 = "Use the same authorized oracle key for both cryptographic operations, with distinct signatures: embedded signature authenticates existing oracle-tagged body; outer activity.signature authenticates the complete normal activity preimage including new payload hash, network, actor, account sequence, fee and validity interval. Retain equality of authority.verified_key, activity.authority and the permitted oracle key. No relayer authorization expansion."
ac_4 = "Keep lx_perps_module_iface() returning ABI1 exactly. Add explicit ABI2 interface with separate decode entrypoint: it accepts transport1 only for oracle ordinal3 and protocol3; all other module ordinals retain existing semantics. ABI1 never starts accepting new137-byte payloads."
ac_5 = "Add canonical signed-genesis governance parameter perps-oracle-transport with zero-padded32-byte key and32-byte value whose only supported present value is1. Absent selects legacy ABI1. Present requires protocol3 and Perps enabled, selects ABI2; wrong module, noncanonical value, duplicate, unsupported protocol, disabled Perps or malformed padding refuses."
ac_6 = "Resolve the selected Perps interface from the signed manifest in the single existing genesis module-plan resolver, keeping the module-table row and default plan legacy. All builder, daemon, guarantor, archive-codec and materialization consumers already call that resolver; selected plans must match registrations, receipt module_version and signed genesis roots. Do not register both interfaces at the same epoch or change old signed module tables."
ac_7 = "Add explicit bootstrap --perps-oracle-transport 1 option which inserts the canonical parameter in sorted order and correct count before normal genesis signing/build. Default bootstrap output stays legacy. Reject the option for a disabled Perps module. No environment-variable-only consensus switch or local replay override."
ac_8 = "New adapter API/config explicitly selects protocol3 and transport1, takes signing key and bounded envelope validity interval, creates the normal outer signature after complete payload construction, and invokes existing adapter_run production flow. Keep old encoder available for historical codec consumers; adapter_run must not emit oracle-only outer signatures. Do not infer protocol from the compile-time default2."
ac_9 = "Envelope validity bounds are explicit, ordered, checked for overflow and within existing maximum window; observation freshness remains checked against recorded batch timestamp. Do not widen staleness/deviation/bounds or modify fee semantics. Use real funded fee balance and positive bounded fee_limit."
ac_10 = "Decode embedded body canonically; pass only its72 bytes to unchanged lx_oracle_key_set_check, keep allowlist, freshness, future-time refusal, bounds, monotonic observation sequence and deviation checks in their existing order, and persist the existing oracle state/event only after all checks."
ac_11 = "Generic activity signature verification, authority resolution, ingress and replay validation remain unchanged. Legacy oracle-only signatures still fail generic verification; separately envelope-signed legacy oracle bodies retain their historical ABI1 module refusal. Never reinterpret such old bytes as valid v2 traffic."
ac_12 = "Preserve ABI1 terminal-rejection replay for both legacy72-byte and formerly invalid137-byte bodies; exact historical result, receipt bytes, module_version and resulting root must survive real daemon restart. ABI2 is selected only in a separately signed activated genesis. Do not infer that old rejected history is absent."
ac_13 = "Keep replay entirely independent of external observation polling: replay consumes authenticated recorded activity bytes, recorded module ABI and original batch timestamp. Verify decoder/signer linkage does not introduce socket or polling dependencies into modules, ledger, state or protocol."
ac_14 = "Owned task driver uses unchanged RuntimeFixture lifecycle, common client and existing canonical foundation producer. A task-owned RuntimeFixture subclass may override only produce() to append the explicit bootstrap activation argument before calling super for a newly created genesis; the legacy scenario uses unmodified bootstrap. No hand-built signed manifest or patching live state."
ac_15 = "Use the existing actual custody funding path: real native deposit transaction, checked deposit event/beneficiary/asset/amount, finalized height, authenticated light-credit proof and signed BRIDGE_CREDIT through native LNI. Read committed main balance before any fee-paying Perps operation."
ac_16 = "Market quote asset must be the genesis custody asset already bound to system:insurance. Fund insurance from legitimately credited owner balance using the existing authorized native transfer path; verify exact debit, credit, asset and conservation via authenticated state reads. Do not mint an unrelated token or inject balances. If no existing permitted transfer can credit insurance, stop with the exact interface gap before changing any authority rule."
ac_17 = "Driver creates market using real signed administrator activity, records actual market account IDs and permitted oracle key, then invokes lx_oracle_adapter_run with owned signed observation input and a real Unix-socket submit callback. No direct module dispatch, private KV writes, replay files as submitted-success substitutes or fabricated receipts in runtime cases."
ac_18 = "Positive runtime observation must result in authenticated successful receipt and signed state proof for the expected stored market/price/time/sequence/source/key, with production fees charged. Repeat exact committed bytes before and after clean and killed-process restarts; assert original receipt and unchanged oracle state/balance after retry."
ac_19 = "Negative runtime cases separate bad outer signature from bad embedded signature, disallowed key, key mismatch, wrong actor/network/protocol, malformed/truncated/overlong body, version0/unknown, zero required fields, stale/future time, out-of-range price, over-deviation, duplicate/regressed sequence, expired outer interval, insufficient fee and incorrect genesis activation. Verify no oracle state mutation; assert admission refusal versus terminal receipt and exact fee/sequence effects according to existing production rules rather than assuming every rejection is free."
ac_20 = "The owned transport fixture signs explicit deterministic observation inputs with its real authorized oracle key. This qualifies transport and authorization behavior; independent live market-feed provenance remains a separate integration obligation."
ac_21 = "Produce all source/digest-bound binaries in one explicit build phase from clean committed source, including fresh canonical six executable/three-WASM bundle and common client. Gate executes prebuilt targets only, fails on missing/stale artifacts and records no skips."
ac_22 = "Qualification consists of exactly one focused gate, with named component, actual-daemon, legacy-replay, activation and negative cases. Record source revision, source tree, exact commands, exits, logs and case-level counts; missing runtime funding or signing prerequisites fail and keep task in_progress."
ac_23 = "Task4.2 retains its full original acceptance and component assertions; consume the qualified oracle transport before executing its real-daemon exchange lifecycle. Rebuild affected artifacts against the selected source and preserve legacy behavior."

